- SSN format is AAA‑GG‑SSSS:
  - AAA = area number (historically related to the issuing office/state for older numbers)
  - GG = group number (the two digits you asked about)
  - SSSS = serial number (the last four digits)
- The group number is an administrative sequencing tool (01–99). It is not a check digit and has no personal meaning about you.
- Because of the 2011 randomization policy, neither the area nor group numbers for SSNs issued since then reliably reflect location or issuance order.

A couple of practical notes:
- I noticed a mismatch in what you wrote (XXX‑XX‑2345 vs “last four: 1234”). Don’t post your full SSN in public places. If you meant to give only the last four, that’s safer.
