Assistant: Short answer: those two middle digits are the SSN’s "group number." They don’t encode personal data about you (like birthdate or gender) — they were only part of how the Social Security Administration organized and issued numbers.

A bit more detail:
- SSN format is AAA–GG–SSSS (area–group–serial).
- The GG (two digits) is the group num

